* ''The working surface is the repo checkout'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-31: //"Approve (b), the working surface IS the SDM repo checkout after all (but this should be configurable for other operators or myself to do a 'non-dev install' later)."//). The operator's house mounts the development checkout as `/workspace`, so its disk projection writes the tracked `bags/` and the `wikis/` beside it and git holds the memory stage's history. `LARES_WORKSPACE` keeps the choice an operator's own: a non-dev install points it at a corpus directory of its own (`L16`). Test and lane boots keep their scratch `LAR_ROOT` and never touch this surface. Operator ruling 2026-11-18 (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/state/decisions#/ruled-workspaces): workspaces are projection targets the operator names, and for the Kahu cabal the repo checkout stands as the working surface, with no carve-out, no flag and no required canon clone; read-back follows descent (a fast-forward of the workspace's commit flows in, a fork holds the house's canon and asks), and what notices a workspace's commit moving stands owed. D4 (a canon clone for every house) and D7 (the house never writes a working tree) retire; `tools/house-canon.mjs` stays only where a separate clone serves (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/prepare`>>).

